--- !u!114 &4682025238987324131
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '<b>Materials</b> are used to set the visual aspect of objects in the Scene. A <b>Material</b> relies on a <b>Shader</b> with a variety of inputs, such as textures and numerical values.


      URP offers a wide range of Shaders such as <b>Lit</b>  and <b>Unlit.</b> You can also create your own shaders, by using <b>Shader Graph</b> for instance.


      For its <b>Lit Shader,</b> URP uses a <b>Physically Based Rendering (PBR)</b> approach. PBR is an industry-standard technique that more accurately tries to simulate the real-world interaction of lighting with surfaces.'
--- !u!114 &7949470957736999023
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "With the help of <b>Shader Graph,</b> URP can easily simulate more advanced materials with translucency and subsurface scattering, as observed, for instance, on vegetation materials.\n\n1. Click a palm tree prefab, and select its LOD0, for instance <b>Palm_2_LOD0.</b>\n\n2. In the <i>Inspector,</i> expand the <b>PalmAtlas_MAT</b> Material.\n\n3. Uncheck the <b>SSS Enabled</b> property. Notice how the light does not travel through the leaves anymore. \n\n4. Undo your change.\n\n5. In the header of the <b>PalmAtlas_MAT</b> material, click the <i>Edit</i> button to open the corresponding <b>Shader Graph.</b>\n\n6. Study how this shader was built.\n\nFor instance, the wind effect is created by animating the position of vertices in the <b>Vertex</b> shader using a Gradient Noise.\n\nThe subsurface scattering, on the other hand, relies on the <b>Emission</b> input in the <b>Fragment</b> shader."
